From caa6ad57c1751dd8e6d146a7deab01ab2c51e5bd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
Date: Mon, 16 Nov 2026 11:16:46 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] media: i2c: add Giantec GT9764BA bidirectional lens actuator

Expose V4L2 focus control and a lens media entity with runtime PM.
Park toward the neutral DAC value 512 before disabling supplies, rather
than driving the bidirectional actuator toward zero as DW9768 does.

The initialization sequence comes from the Piano OS3.0.309.0.WPYCNXM
factory actuator module description. Its OEM park callback uses 50-code
steps with 10000 us command delays. The published GPL GT9764 driver also
parks at 512:
https://github.com/MiCode/Xiaomi_Kernel_OpenSource/blob/a369d30bd5df3fcfb4304ee9e7ae10fa4f11899a/drivers/misc/mediatek/lens/vcm/v4l2/gt9764/gt9764.c

Use the factory AAC register bytes without applying the incompatible
DW9768 timing formula. The 10 ms ramp delay is a parking sequence delay,
not a claim about optical settling after a focus change. Keep the lens
powered if parking fails.

Signed-off-by: slwyts <slwyts@foxmail.com>
---
